### Case: token-issue — exchange client credentials for a signed JWT.
### The client id is the app's credential KEY. The secret is the credential SECRET.
### Sending the secret where the id belongs is the most common cause of a
### surprising 401 here.
### Expect 200 with access_token / token_type / expires_in.
POST {{GATEWAY}}/oauth/token
authorization: Basic {{BASE64(CLIENT_ID:CLIENT_SECRET)}}
content-type: application/json

### curl equivalent (curl does the base64 for you):
###   curl -i -X POST {{GATEWAY}}/oauth/token \
###     -u '{{CLIENT_ID}}:{{CLIENT_SECRET}}' \
###     -H 'content-type: application/json'
